+Receipt `doc/benchmarks/2026-10-08-math-chain-repair/` (measured source 733
+files, canonical map `f944bef3…`; integrity, helper and first-receipt
+checks all match). The default sweep is green (5,319 passed, 284 skipped,
+one XPASS), the thinking gate 57/57, the standing thirty 10/10 throughout
+with zero thought entry, and the ten paired starts have distinct fresh RNG
+archives and bit-identical initial choosers across their three conditions;
+no seed, no retry. **All thirty declared attempts failed inside epoch
+one** — after 0 to 162 of the epoch's 1,449 sentences, nine of the ten
+zero-budget attempts within 25 seconds — so, as in §12, held-out binding,
+chain success and chooser displacement are unavailable, not zero. The
+receipt says so correctly and claims nothing. Not accepted; no learning
+claim; both receipts are retained as they are.
+
+Of the five repairs: the shared LTM with batch-sized priming reads, the
+retired position filter, `ltmCapacity` over `truthMaxEntries` with a
+fail-loud full store, and the pending relational row are delivered with
+mechanism tests. `bind()` is delivered as a method `interpret` calls, with
+mint and open scored by the shared chooser (a `reference_choice` feature,
+near-uniform at start). The `isPart` filter validates occupied operands
+only and keeps grammar-open forms; the stated contract (both operands
+accepted concepts) was not delivered and no reason is given — deliver it
+or the reason.
